==Detecting Weak Points==
Some effects will visually highlight specific Weak Points for the player:
*{{A|Seek}} highlights some Weak Points (see [[Seek#Bugs]]).
*{{Weapon|Zenith}}'s Alt-Fire highlights heads.
*{{Weapon|Scourge}}'s Alt-Fire highlights heads.
*{{Weapon|Vesper 77}}'s aim highlights heads.

==Notes==
*Certain weapons do not have bonus damage on headshots, always defaulting to the 1x multiplier, unaffected by acuity-like bonuses but affected by deadhead-like bonuses:
**{{Weapon|Arca Plasmor}} ({{Weapon|Tenet Arca Plasmor|Tenet}})
**{{Weapon|Alternox}}'s primary fire ({{Weapon|Alternox Prime}})
**{{Weapon|Argo & Vel}}'s Heavy Attack Glaive
**{{Weapon|Athodai}}'s Alternate Fire
**{{Weapon|Catchmoon}}
**{{Weapon|Catchmoon (Secondary)}}
**{{Weapon|Corufell}}'s shots
**{{Weapon|Cyanex}}'s Primary Fire
**{{Resource|Dread Incarnon Genesis}}
**{{Weapon|Fulmin}} in semi-auto mode
**{{Weapon|Ignis}} ({{Weapon|Ignis Wraith}})
**{{Resource|Lex Incarnon Genesis}}
**{{Weapon|Lizzie}}'s Primary Fire and Waves
**{{Weapon|Nataruk}}'s charged and perfect shots
**{{Weapon|Nepheri}}'s Fireballs
**{{Resource|Paris Incarnon Genesis}}
**{{Weapon|Steflos}}
**{{Weapon|Stropha}}'s shots
**{{Weapon|Tenet Agendus}}'s Energy Disks
**{{D|Electricity}} and {{D|Gas}} status procs
**Resupply
*Most Headshot bonuses stack their effects additively. For example, a {{Weapon|Daikyu}} using {{Arcane|Primary Deadhead}} and {{M|Amalgam Daikyu Target Acquired}} on an enemy with a 3x headshot multiplier will have a {{Math|3 * (1 + {{Arcane|Primary Deadhead|30%}} + {{M|Amalgam Daikyu Target Acquired|75%}})|b=y|bf=y}}x headshot multiplier.
*Radial parts of all [[Area of Effect Weapons]] have a 1x headshot multiplier and additionally cannot trigger headshot conditions.
**This does not apply to the projectile itself, such as {{Weapon|Kuva Bramma}}'s arrows or {{Weapon|Kuva Chakkhurr}}'s precision shots.

==Patch History==
{{Scrollbox/Article|
{{ver|39}}
*Fixed instances of “Weak Points” being written as “weakpoints”.

{{ver|32}}
;Headshot Damage Changes

During playtesting, the ammo changes alone weren’t enough to significantly change things for AoE weapons. So instead of tightening these values to be overly restrictive, we chose to address other factors that make these weapons so strong, such as headshot damage. 

Our approach here is two-fold, to reduce the impact of headshots for AOE weapons, but to also make precision headshots pack a larger punch overall.

*Radial damage no longer gains extra headshot damage or triggers headshot conditions.
**This is primarily targeted at the Ignis Wraith - as a “flamethrower” weapon, it’s hard to imagine a blanket of elements being precise enough to target weak points specifically. Explosive projectiles themselves can still land headshots, so there is still a reason to aim with most weapons for maximum damage.
*Increased the base damage multiplier on headshots from 2x to 3x. 
**This means precision weapons are more rewarded for skillful usage, leveling the playing field even further!

{{ver|21}}
*Corpus Ospreys can now receive headshots! You may now unleash devastating shots to their “faces”.
}}

